{
  "dom_id": "step-q10195",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that  $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\ny+2=1\\,\u27f9\\,y=1-2=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-1$into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-1)+(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}-2+1=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $y=-1$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e8-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2\u27e9.$",
